  "prompt_text": "The figure sketches two parallel registers of qubits, labeled \\(A\\) qubits on the top row and \\(B\\) qubits on the bottom row, arranged site by site across a chain from 1 to \\(N\\). Each qubit is drawn as a blue Bloch-sphere-like icon with the same arrow orientation, suggesting a repeated local two-qubit structure at every position. The middle of the diagram highlights one representative “\\(j\\)th site,” enclosed in a box, to indicate that the same construction applies uniformly across the system.\n\nBeneath this highlighted pair, two operators are shown. One acts only on the \\(A\\) qubit at that site while leaving the \\(B\\) qubit unchanged, written as something like \\(Q_1 = X_A \\otimes 1_B\\). The second applies the same Pauli-\\(X\\) action to both qubits in the pair, \\( \\tilde Q_1 = X_A \\otimes X_B\\). Taken together, the image conveys a comparison between local operators on a two-layer qubit architecture: one acting on a single subsystem and one acting jointly on both subsystems at the same site. The ellipses indicate this pattern repeats for many sites along the chain.",
